  "plan": {
    "goal": "Culture human proximal tubular epithelial cells in a microchannel reproducing the in vivo apical fluid shear of ~0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa).",
    "rationale": "PTEC apical shear target of 0.2 dyn/cm² = 0.02 Pa (user-specified physiological value; PTEC not in the physiology registry, so this target is treated as unverified and should be confirmed against literature). A 1000 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm rectangular channel was chosen as a proximal-tubule-like lumen. Using the flow-rate-for-shear inverse calculator, 2.0 µL/min gives exactly 0.02 Pa (0.2 dyn/cm²) at culture-medium viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s. Flow is laminar (Re ≈ 0.06), pressure drop is negligible (~8 Pa), and residence time is ~60 s. Cells are seeded at 5e4 cells/cm² (typical epithelial seeding density) over the 0.2 cm² channel floor → 10,000 cells. Culture medium viscosity assumed water-like (1e-3 Pa·s).",
